            <ArticleTitle>Pain relief with intravenous regional guanethedine in post-traumatic reflex sympathetic dystrophy--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>236-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intravenous regional guanethedine (IVRG), using the Bier's block technique, was given to relieve pain in a 62 year old Indian woman suffering from reflex sympathetic dystrophy. The patient obtained complete pain relief with 2 injections and has remained pain-free for 18 months.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
